somes by yIF2, a bacterial IF2 homolog in yeast</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1998</year><volume>280</volume><fpage>1757</fpage><lpage>1760</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9624054</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cobucci-Ponzano</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The gene of an archaeal alpha-<sc>l</sc>-fucosidase is expressed by translational frameshifting</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>4258</fpage><lpage>4268</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16920738</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Condo</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Cis</italic>-acting signals controlling translational initiation in the thermophilic archaeon <italic>Sulfolobus solfataricus</italic></article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>384</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10564480</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elish</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biochemical analysis of spontaneous <italic>fepA</italic> mutants of <italic>Escherichia coli</italic></article-title><source>J Gen Microbiol</source><year>1988</year><volume>134</volume><fpage>1355</fpage><lpage>1364</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3058866</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gualerzi</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Initiation of mRNA translation in prokaryotes</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>1990</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>5881